WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:05.520
Fans and critics alike have already started
to weigh in on Adam Warlock's looks in the

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.780
"Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3" trailer.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.230
Here's how he stacks up to his comic book
counterpart.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:16.939
The long-awaited debut of the "Guardians of
the Galaxy Vol. 3" movie trailer has finally

00:00:16.939 --> 00:00:20.400
come and has already garnered millions of
YouTube views.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.900
And there are a lot of revealing bits of story
packed into just under two minutes.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:29.420
There's a strong hint that many of the main
characters will meet a fatal end and the introduction

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:32.489
of Lylla, a fan-favorite character from the
comics.

00:00:32.489 --> 00:00:36.760
But the debut of another comic book character
that fans have been waiting for since "Guardians

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:42.740
of the Galaxy Vol. 2" debuted in 2017 is probably
the biggest reveal.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:47.139
That character is none other than Adam Warlock,
played by Will Poulter.

00:00:47.139 --> 00:00:52.809
"I think I shall call him…Adam."

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:58.535
There's a ton of hype for the film as a whole,
but the chatter around Warlock is particularly positive.

00:00:58.535 --> 00:01:03.510
Many fans are eager for the emotional payoff
they've been waiting almost six years for.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:08.090
What they may not know, however, is that adapting
Warlock from the comics in a way that would

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:12.280
please moviegoers and comic book fans alike
is a tall ask.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:17.049
Thanks to his many rebirths in the comics,
Adam Warlock has had more costume changes

00:01:17.049 --> 00:01:20.049
than even the most seasoned X-Men veteran.

00:01:20.049 --> 00:01:24.830
From the brief look we get, it's clear that
Warlock will be wearing his red uniform with

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:26.799
a skull affixed to the collar.

00:01:26.799 --> 00:01:32.270
This is the costume he wore after being resurrected
to defeat Thanos and protect half of all life

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:36.479
in the universe from being blinked out of
existence by the Infinity Gauntlet.

00:01:36.479 --> 00:01:40.409
It makes sense that the studio would go with
this look since that's also the arc where

00:01:40.409 --> 00:01:45.689
he has the most interaction with Nebula, Gamora,
and Drax, all of whom will be returning for

00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:48.000
"GotG Volume 3."

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.980
So far, the vast majority of fans are in favor
of this choice.

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:57.030
Several Redditors think the makeup has improved
since the last film; and although other commenters

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:00.670
don't see much of a difference at all, they
agree it looks good and fits well with the

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:02.420
sci-fi tone of the film.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:04.670
But not everyone is as optimistic.

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:09.619
Even though there's a ton of praise for Warlock's
split-second appearance in this appreciation

00:02:09.619 --> 00:02:11.810
thread for the trailer, one user said,

00:02:15.341 --> 00:02:19.840
But the top comment from Reddit expressing
enthusiasm for Warlock's presence in the trailer

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.540
has hundreds of upvotes so far, so it's safe
to assume that the look he'll be sporting

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:28.610
in the MCU will go over well with the majority
of audiences.

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:32.300
Those who have viewed the trailer saw Warlock
for no more than a second, and in that brief

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:36.660
amount of time, all we see is a brief shot
of his face from the shoulders up, as well

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:40.560
as him seemingly punching a downed Nebula
hard in the head.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.590
If you pay close enough attention, you can
see the skull decoration on the movie version

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:49.250
of his suit, albeit it's muted to blend in
rather than standing out prominently as it

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.590
does in the comics.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:54.590
He's also sporting a very powerful soul gem
on his forehead, and it does appear as though

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:56.610
he still has his red cape.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:00.790
Fans and critics alike are impressed with
how Warlock looks in the trailer.

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:05.019
Prominent movie critic Tessa Smith at Rotten
Tomatoes, in a longer tweet about the overall

00:03:05.019 --> 00:03:07.690
impression the trailer made on her, she said,

00:03:13.116 --> 00:03:17.980
With the warm reception Warlock has received
so far, it would be a surprise if fans ended

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:22.612
up hating him after seeing him make his big
MCU debut in theaters next year.

